## Execution order — validations and side-effects

### 0. Security pre-check (before method body)
`@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` — caller must hold the OWNER_ADMIN role, else 403 (see `handleAccessDeniedException` re-throw in the advice).

### 1. Bean Validation on the request body (before the method runs)
The interface param is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (in `OwnersApi.addOwner`, and the interface is `@Validated`). Constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java`), which are enforced first and produce a 400 via `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`:

- `firstName`: `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName`: `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `title`: `@Size(max = 30)`
- `address`: `@Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `addressLine1`: `@Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `addressLine2`: `@Size(max = 255)`
- `city`: `@NotNull` `@Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- `telephone`: `@NotNull` `@Size(min = 1, max = 20)`
- `email`: `@Size(min = 1, max = 255)` `@jakarta.validation.constraints.Email`
- `registrationDate`: `@Valid` (LocalDate)
- `sharesHousehold`: none
- `postcode`: `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{4}$")`
- `birthDate`: `@Valid` (LocalDate)

Note: the DTO-level `@Pattern`/`@Size`/`@Email` constraints are validated by the framework before `addOwner` executes, in addition to the controller's own hand-rolled checks below (which are stricter/different). There is a custom validator in the project (`PetAgeValidation`/`PetAgeValidator` under `rest/validation/`) but it applies to pets only — it is NOT referenced by any owner field.

### 2. Idempotency short-circuit (lines 746-755)
`currentIdempotencyKey()` reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header (via `RequestContextHolder`). If present and already in the process-wide `idempotencyKeys` map (a `ConcurrentHashMap<String,Integer>`), it looks up the previously created owner (`findOwnerById`) and returns it with **200 OK**, skipping creation entirely.

### 3. Address normalization — `applyAddress` (line 756; impl 221-234)
Mutates the DTO in place. Uses `normalizeAddress` (179-203): trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand tokens `ST→STREET`, `RD→ROAD`, `AVE→AVENUE`. Prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` over flat `address`; writes normalized `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` back (null if empty) and sets composed `address`.

### 4. Required-field check — `validateRequiredFields` (line 757; impl 142-162)
Blank/null check (`isBlank`) on `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (the composed value from step 3), `city`, `telephone`. Any missing → `RequiredFieldsMissingException` → **400** with an `errors` array of field names.

### 5. Registration date handling (lines 758-766)
- Null → defaults to `LocalDate.now()`.
- After today → `FutureRegistrationDateException` → **400** (`errors: [registrationDate]`).
- Then `toBusinessDay` (523-530) rolls Saturdays/Sundays and fixed 2026 public holidays (`PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS`, 510-513) forward to the next business day. Result written back to DTO.

### 6. Daily-owner-limit check — `rejectDailyOwnerLimit` (line 767; impl 475-483)
Calls `clinicService.findAllOwners()`, counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals the effective date; if `>= DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT (100)` → `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` → **429**.

### 7. City-capacity check — `rejectCityAtCapacity` (line 768; impl 448-457)
`findAllOwners()`, counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive, trimmed); if `>= CITY_CAPACITY (50)` → `CityAtCapacityException` → **409**.

### 8. Postcode validation — `validatePostcode` (line 769; impl 699-715)
If postcode present: must match `\d{4}` else `InvalidPostcodeException` → **400**. If the city maps to a region (`CITY_REGION`: Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD), the postcode must be within that region's range (`REGION_POSTCODES`: NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099), else `InvalidPostcodeException` → **400**.

### 9. Telephone normalization — `normalizeTelephone` (lines 770-771; impl 250-273)
Strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps `+`+country code, else assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0`. Must be `+` followed by 8-15 digits. Country-specific national length enforced: `+61`→9 national digits, `+1`→10 (`requireNationalLength`, 284-290). Failure → `InvalidTelephoneException` → **400** (`errors: [telephone]`). Normalized E.164 value written back to DTO. (This is stricter than and separate from the DTO's `@Size` and the entity `@Pattern`.)

### 10. Email normalization — `normalizeEmail` (lines 772-773; impl 300-314)
Null/blank → null. Otherwise must match `EMAIL_PATTERN` (`^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$`) else `InvalidEmailException` → **400**. Lower-cased. Domain checked against `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) → `InvalidEmailException` → **400** (`errors: [email]`). Written back to DTO.

### 11. Household id + duplicate/identity checks (lines 774-779)
- `sharesHousehold` = `Boolean.TRUE.equals(dto.getSharesHousehold())`.
- `householdId` (428-431) = first 12 hex of SHA-256 of `normalizedLastName + "|" + postcode`.
- `rejectDuplicateIdentity` (356-364): builds `identityKey` = `telephone|email|householdId` (`deriveIdentityKey`, 328-332); over `activeOwners()` (non-soft-deleted, 351-354) via `findAllOwners()`, if any existing owner's derived key matches → `DuplicateIdentityException` → **409** (`errors: [identityKey]`).
- `rejectDuplicateHousehold` (377-387): unless `sharesHousehold`, if any active owner shares the same `householdId` → `DuplicateHouseholdException` → **409** (`errors: [lastName, address]`).
- `findPossibleDuplicateOf` (401-414): soft-match only when not `sharesHousehold` — same last name (case-insensitive) + same postcode + different telephone; returns the lowest matching owner id, else null.

Note: `DuplicateTelephoneException` and `DuplicateEmailException` have handlers in the advice but are NOT thrown anywhere in the create path anymore — those checks were consolidated into the single identity-key check.

### 12. Entity mapping — `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` (line 781)
MapStruct mapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (`toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`, lines 337-347). Ignores `id, pets, customerCode, householdId, namesakeCount, bulkSignupWarning, householdSize, possibleDuplicate, possibleDuplicateOf, deleted` (these are set explicitly next). Generated impl at `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/annotations/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapperImpl.java`.

### 13. Derived fields set on the entity (lines 782-789)
- `possibleDuplicate` = (possibleDuplicateOf != null); `possibleDuplicateOf`.
- `customerCode` = `deduplicateCustomerCode(customerCode(postcode, telephone, lastName))`. `customerCode` (545-547) = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` where REGION via `regionFromPostcode` and HASH8 = first 8 upper hex of SHA-256(`telephone+lastName`). `deduplicateCustomerCode` (558-573) scans all owners' codes and appends `-<n>` (n≥2) if collision.
- `householdId`; `householdSize` (652-659) = 1 + count of active... actually count of all owners with same householdId + 1.
- `namesakeCount` (632-640) = count of owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).
- `bulkSignupWarning` (502-507) = true if owners already registered on the effective date `> BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD (80)`.

All of steps 6, 7, 11, 13 issue their own `findAllOwners()` calls (multiple full-table scans per create).

### 14. Persist — `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (line 790)
Service `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`, `saveOwner` at 232-237, annotated `@Transactional` (read-write) — this is the transaction boundary for the write. It delegates to `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.

Repository (jpa profile) `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `save` at 92-100: `em.persist(owner)` when id is null, else `em.merge(owner)`. (A JDBC impl also exists: `repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, active under the `jdbc` profile.)

There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks or listeners: no `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@PreUpdate`/`@PostLoad`, no `@EntityListeners`, no `AuditingEntityListener`, no `@EventListener`/`@TransactionalEventListener`, and no `@PostConstruct` anywhere in `src`. On save, Hibernate flush also re-checks the entity's own Bean Validation constraints (`Owner`: `@NotEmpty` on `address`, `city`, `telephone` + `@Pattern("^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$")` on `telephone`; `Person`: `@NotEmpty` on `firstName`, `lastName` — files `model/Owner.java`, `model/Person.java`).

The one aspect in the project, `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CallMonitoringAspect.java` (`@Aspect`, `@Around("within(@org.springframework.stereotype.Repository *)")`), wraps every `@Repository` call (including the save and all the `findAll` scans) purely to accumulate JMX call-count/timing. No business effect.

### 15. Idempotency record (lines 791-793)
If an idempotency key was supplied, `idempotencyKeys.put(key, owner.getId())` stores the new id for future replays.

### 16. Audit logging (lines 794-796)
Emits an INFO line on the dedicated `"AUDIT"` SLF4J logger with `id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber`. `membershipLevel`/`membershipNumber` are computed on the fly by the mapper (see below). No external/email/notification calls exist anywhere in the flow — the only side channels are this audit log line and the JMX aspect counter.

### 17. Response mapping and 201 (lines 797-800)
`ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` computes many read-only derived fields via `@Mapping(... expression=...)` (OwnerMapper 22-37): `salutation, displayName, initials, telephoneDisplay, membershipNumber, checkDigit, membershipPoints, membershipLevel, locality, timezone, contactPreference, identityKey, ageBand, fiscalYear, selfLink`. `Location` header set to `/api/owners/{id}`. Returns **201 CREATED**.

